            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Desda"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! Served with fresh green beans one day with company and grilled artichokes another. I used all the ingredients but a lot more of the seasonings, especially the horseradish and Worcestershire-probably tripled them. I didn’t want it to taste like slightly seasoned mayo.",
            "datePublished": "2018-07-14T00:04:34.723Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ctmamacooks"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This sauce is a great complement to all summer vegetables, as well as chicken or beef. Great exactly as directed, it also lends itself easily to a multitude of slight substitutions. I omitted the Worcester sauce, instead adding fresh garlic &amp; fresh mixed herbs, Dijon mustard and a splash of white wine. Instead of mashing by hand, I whipped it all together in my Ninja....adding just a drizzle of EVOO to emulsify. Delish! You can't go wrong either following the instructions verbatim, or playing with your personal favorite additions. A win!",
            "datePublished": "2017-07-26T22:33:34.743Z"
          },
          {
